<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/3rd-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">First Macedonian War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">214–<a href="/years/205-bce">205 BCE</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century-bce">3rd century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The First Macedonian War was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-v-of-macedon">Philip V of Macedon</a>, who had allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hannibal">Hannibal</a> during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-punic-war">Second Punic War</a>. Rome left most of the fighting to its Greek allies of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aetolian-league">Aetolian League</a>, while Roman fleets raided the coasts, sacking Dyme in 208 BCE. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-phoenice">Peace of Phoenice</a> in 205 BCE ended the war without decisive result.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-macedonian-war.jpg" alt="First Macedonian War" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Goran tek-en translator: Manlleus (ca) · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mediterranean_at_218_BC-en.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
